{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA: sync MCP tool offloading currently uses anyio.to_thread.run_sync with abandon_on_cancel=False, so a client-canceled call keeps its request coroutine attached to the worker and holds the default worker-limiter token until the sync body returns. A burst of canceled long searches can fill the limiter and queue a later simple read until the tools/call deadline. The fix should alter offload cancellation semantics, not add new store locks or search-specific throttles."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788893204049564001,"uuid":"70a110c7-ade5-4852-8464-843790b4d178"}